  ctaText="If your Tampa firm is paying for SEO, ads, directories and an answering service and still can't name its cost per retained client, that is the conversation worth having."
>
  <p class="lm-lede">Search "legal marketing Tampa" and you'll find page after page of agencies offering SEO, pay-per-click, websites and social media. Almost all of them sell execution. Very few of them will tell you, in dollars, what it cost your firm to sign its last ten clients.</p>

  <p>That number is what we work on. Hughey LLC is an independent <a href="/">law firm marketing consultancy</a> with more than 20 years spent exclusively in legal marketing. We don't run your ads, build your website or sell you a content package. We sit above the vendors you already have, connect their work to signed retainers, and help you put your budget where it actually produces cases.</p>

  <h2>The Tampa Legal Market Is Crowded at the Top of the Funnel</h2>

  <div class="lm-facts">
    <div class="lm-fact"><span>Courts</span><strong>Thirteenth Judicial Circuit, Hillsborough County</strong></div>
    <div class="lm-fact"><span>Firm clusters</span><strong>Downtown, Westshore, Channel District</strong></div>
    <div class="lm-fact"><span>Search overlap</span><strong>Tampa, St. Pete and Clearwater in one bay market</strong></div>
    <div class="lm-fact"><span>Big-firm pressure</span><strong>National and statewide brands bid on local terms</strong></div>
  </div>

  <p>Tampa is home to some of Florida's largest firms, a deep bench of mid-size litigation shops, and hundreds of small and boutique practices. Heavy advertisers in personal injury push up the cost of visibility for everyone who shares their search results, maps listings and directory placements, including family law, employment and estate planning firms that never run a billboard.</p>

  <p>The result is a market where it is easy to buy leads and hard to know which leads turn into clients. Firms add a new channel every time a vendor makes a good pitch, and nobody owns the question of whether the whole system is working.</p>

  <h2>Where Tampa Firms Lose Money</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Agencies grading their own homework.</strong> Your SEO vendor reports rankings, your ads vendor reports clicks and your directory reports calls. None of them reports signed retainers, and none has a reason to.</li>
    <li><strong>Overlapping geo-targeting.</strong> Tampa, St. Petersburg, Clearwater and the I-4 corridor share one media market. Firms that target all of it without checking where clients actually come from often pay twice for the same searcher.</li>
    <li><strong>Leakage between the call and the consult.</strong> Slow callbacks, after-hours voicemail and web forms nobody owns lose qualified people before a lawyer ever speaks to them. That money was already spent.</li>
    <li><strong>Directories and Local Services Ads with no attribution.</strong> Most firms can tell you what they pay for these placements. Very few can tie them to fees collected.</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising that ignores the Florida Bar.</strong> Florida's lawyer advertising rules are among the strictest in the country. An agency built for dentists and roofers will not always write copy that respects them, and your license is the one at risk.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="lm-pull">The question isn't whether your marketing is busy. It's what each channel costs per retained client, and nobody in your vendor stack is paid to answer it.</p>

  <h2>What We Do for Tampa Law Firms</h2>

  <ol class="lm-steps">
    <li><h3>Audit the whole stack</h3><p>Every vendor, platform, tracking number and intake step, mapped in one place so you can see what is connected and what isn't. <a href="/services/strategic-marketing-for-law-firms/">More on strategy engagements</a>.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Build the cost-per-retained-client view</h3><p>Ad spend, calls, forms, consults and signed matters tied together by channel, so budget decisions stop being guesses. <a href="/services/data-analysis-for-law-firms/">See data analysis</a>.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Hold agencies accountable</h3><p>One set of KPIs every vendor reports against, with regular reviews that ask what their work produced in signed clients. <a href="/services/agency-management-for-law-firms/">See agency management</a>.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Fix intake</h3><p>Response times, qualification, follow-up and handoff to the attorney, redesigned so the leads you already pay for become consults. <a href="/services/intake-process-optimization/">See intake optimization</a>.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Run a 12-month plan</h3><p>A written plan tied to retained-client targets, reviewed monthly, that scales what works and cuts what doesn't.</p></li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Why Tampa Firms Choose an Independent Consultancy</h2>

  <p>When your only marketing advisor is also the company selling you marketing, every recommendation comes with a conflict. An independent consultancy has one job: making sure the money you spend turns into clients. That means we'll tell you when a channel should be cut, when an agency is underperforming, and when the problem isn't marketing at all but what happens after the phone rings.</p>

  <p>We work with firms across the <a href="/location/">Tampa Bay area</a>, from our home base in <a href="/florida/st-petersburg/">St. Petersburg</a> to Hillsborough, Pasco and beyond, and with firms throughout <a href="/florida/">Florida</a>.</p>
</LocalMarketPage>
